35,2,1,talk,Shion,,The wall is one sheet of plasterboard. You can hear every word inside. And three keyboards are buried in crumbs.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I see. Sixty-eight thousand yen for nine small bookings. And the quotes are high. I need to understand the costs.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, the tally says the two nearest the door used it eleven times! And the awkward talk happened right at the desks, in front of everyone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, that is a painful truth. When difficult words are spoken in the open, trust fractures. We need a place where honesty can be held gently, without an audience.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Eleven callouts for equipment, zero for the empty store. The hours vanish into maintenance, not use.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, eleven callouts? That is the cost of noise. The plasterboard fails, and the crumbs prove we eat where we work.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, the callouts are high, but the invoices show we already pay for small groups. The quotes are steep. I need to see the total before agreeing.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, that is so sad! If they had a private room, maybe they wouldn’t have gone quiet for two weeks.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, exactly. A fortnight of silence is a heavy price for a lack of privacy. We must build a space where difficult truths can be spoken without fear of judgment.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, the invoices confirm the leak. We pay for small groups, yet the callouts show the equipment fails. The hours are gone.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, the plasterboard is the leak. Sound escapes, crumbs spread. We need a room that actually holds its secrets, not just a box.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I hear you. But the quotes are steep. One is 141,000, the other 96,000. We must be careful with the money.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, I think a quiet room would help! If people can talk without being watched, maybe they won’t go silent for weeks.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, you are right. A quiet room offers shelter, but it must also invite connection. We need a space where silence is comfortable, yet conversation is possible.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, shelter is not the only cost. The callouts prove the equipment eats our hours. We must weigh that against the privacy you seek.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, shelter is not enough. The plasterboard fails, and the crumbs prove we eat where we work. We need a room that actually holds its secrets, not just a box.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
